usage: run_history200.py [-h] [--private-env PRIVATE_ENV]
                         [--window-file WINDOW_FILE]
                         [--expected-head EXPECTED_HEAD] [--output OUTPUT]
                         [--requests REQUESTS] [--seconds SECONDS] [--serve]
                         [--port PORT] [--observer OBSERVER] [--ready READY]
                         [--nonce NONCE]

Bounded local HTTP characterization, never a production load generator.
Explicit invocation only; no latency/SLO assertion. Own migrated PostgreSQL
UUID database, real restricted-role app, real TCP HTTP, no auth/route
overrides. Provider configuration is cleared by tests.isolation before app
imports.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --private-env PRIVATE_ENV
  --window-file WINDOW_FILE
  --expected-head EXPECTED_HEAD
  --output OUTPUT
  --requests REQUESTS
  --seconds SECONDS
  --serve
  --port PORT
  --observer OBSERVER
  --ready READY
  --nonce NONCE
